@@ -2,7 +2,6 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
-
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
 ```
@@ -15,3 +14,37 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+The sign-up page collects account details, sends an SMS, and verifies the six-digit
+code on the server before calling the existing registration service. No test codes
+or simulated SMS success are used when the SMS service is unavailable.
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and supply your Twilio account SID, auth token, and
+Verify service SID. Configure that service to use **six-digit codes** and a
+10-minute validity period. For a deployed Node server, set these environment
+variables at runtime. Credentials stay on the server.
+
+For automatic SMS extraction, configure a domain-bound Verify SMS template as the
+service default, or set `TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID`. The SMS must end with a line
+like `@your-domain.example #123456`, using the actual code and the hostname serving
+the sign-up page. WebOTP requires HTTPS and a supported device/browser; keyboard
+OTP suggestions, pasting, and manual entry are also supported. See
+[Twilio's domain-bound SMS setup](https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/developers/tutorials/product/domain-bound-sms-otps-verify)
+and [Chrome's WebOTP guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp).
+
+Challenges use Astro's server session storage with a ten-minute TTL, five code
+attempts, five SMS requests per active session window, and a 30-second resend
+cooldown. Keep Twilio's provider abuse protections enabled; session limits alone
+do not prevent abuse across fresh sessions. Multi-instance deployments need shared
+session storage instead of the Node adapter's default filesystem storage.
+
+The verified phone is forwarded to the existing external registration API as
+`phone`. Phone persistence and preventing direct, unverified calls to that external
+API must also be enforced by its owner; this repository only controls its own
+sign-up route.
+
+Run `node --test tests/signup.test.mjs` (Node 24+) for mocked provider tests, and
+`pnpm run build` for the production build. Live SMS delivery requires the configured
+Twilio service and is not exercised by these tests.
